msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-setup.rst:5
#: 9acc5eec56c54894b6612f187ebf4b85
msgid "RangeFinders Setup Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-setup.rst:7
#: 95f417cba95c48388c89ca74a2b2c032
msgid "There are many different kinds of rangefinders: Lidar (using laser or infra-red light to measure distance), Sonar (using ultrasonic sound), and Radar (using microwave RF). Some are analog, producing  pulses whose timing represent the distance to an object, others are digital sending data streams over serial to UARTs, or I2C, or even via DroneCAN."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-setup.rst:9
#: ad0f8461da1e4822ae786a6e728ea5ab
msgid ":ref:`RangeFinders (Sonar or Lidar) <common-rangefinder-landingpage>` can be used for :ref:`Object Avoidance <common-object-avoidance-landing-page>` as well as altitude sensors for precision landing in Plane and Copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-setup.rst:15
#: 4e7e9ca539d6490b95cb726c840c6878
msgid ":ref:`common-object-avoidance-landing-page` features are new and should be used with caution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-setup.rst:18
#: 701b452cccbe4b1cb793f9e1dc573430
msgid "Up to 10 Rangefinders can be used in the system (1 thru A). :ref:`Object Avoidance <common-object-avoidance-landing-page>` can use a single 360 degree Lidar, or up to 9 unidirectional rangefinders: 8 arranged in a circle covering 45 degree wide segments, plus an upward facing rangefinder. And a downward facing rangefinder used for low altitude height above ground measurements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-setup.rst:21
#: 536271c3e6fe4be6a4ceac8220ca341c
msgid "Connecting and Configuring the Rangefinder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-setup.rst:23
#: 7dc75af3f4d8461a8aed238d430d513d
msgid "Follow the instructions for each type of rangefinder described in its linked page on :ref:`common-rangefinder-landingpage`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-setup.rst:24
#: b6f7608ca1394cbbacd336d292d9e151
msgid "Set the RNGFNDx_ORIENT parameters (i.e. :ref:`RNGFND1_ORIENT <RNGFND1_ORIENT>`, :ref:`RNGFND2_ORIENT <RNGFND2_ORIENT>`, etc.) to specify the direction each range finder is pointing in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-setup.rst:26
#: cfcb1d98c8654197a15ccb5dcb4d9765
msgid "Note that if the type of rangefinder is set or changed, a reboot will be required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-setup.rst:31
#: 2ca0f8c156dc427cb52e476e89b314f5
msgid "If a rangefinder is oriented facing down, it will  be used to for height above ground measurements when within its range for increased landing precision in Copter, and in Plane autotakeoffs/autolandings, and QuadPlane VTOL operations depending on which bits in the :ref:`RNGFND_LANDING<RNGFND_LANDING>` parameter are set. In Copter, when landing and within 10m of the ground according to the range finder, the vehicle will slow its descent to the :ref:`LAND_SPD_MS<LAND_SPD_MS>` (which defaults to 50cm/s). In Plane, see the \"using a rangefinder\" section of :ref:`automatic-landing`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-setup.rst:33
#: d5488cb235c441c6b151396cf12bfd16
msgid "If using a rangefinder for altitude measurements, be sure to read this page:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-setup.rst:41
#: d68f00f372d546de8e2474924593c5ac
msgid "Only downward facing rangefinders are supported in Plane currently."
msgstr ""

